I give up.

The statement is true. I checked the math by hand: with 0-indexed `X`, `E[S] = Σₙ≥₁ 1/((n+1)!·2ⁿ) = 2√e − 3`. But a Lean proof needs:

- the joint law of finitely many i.i.d. uniforms, obtained from `iIndepFun`;
- the volume of the decreasing-chain region and the integral of its last coordinate;
- exchanging the integral with the `tsum` over the random index set `k ω`, with measurability of `k`;
- a.s. handling of the no-stop case and of `X_i ∈ [0,1]`.

Mathlib has no direct lemmas for these, and only compiled Mathlib is available here, so I cannot search the source to find the right APIs. I did not edit `/work/putnam_2022_a4.lean`, and it still contains the `sorry`.
